  "traditionalForm": "望",
  "additionalMeanings": [],
  "formationType": "simpleIdeograph",
  "visualTeachingNotes": [
    "A person looking upward toward a crescent moon, with an eye shown separately to emphasize looking.",
    "Oracle is a thin standing profile with a small eye- or head-like form projecting to the right near the top.",
    "Regular 望 regularizes the upper 亡/月-related shapes over 王, leaving the original person gazing at the moon readable only through the historical sequence."
  ],
